2
00:00:04,837 --> 00:00:07,506
-Hey.
-Oh, hey. You work the lunch shift?

3
00:00:07,673 --> 00:00:10,425
Yeah. Got 8 pounds of salmon
that's about to go bad.

4
00:00:10,593 --> 00:00:12,678
-Do you know how to cook it?
-Not really.

5
00:00:12,845 --> 00:00:16,557
PENNY: Damn it.
Should've liberated the iffy chicken.

6
00:00:16,766 --> 00:00:20,770
So, what are you
and Professor Fussyface up to tonight?

7
00:00:20,937 --> 00:00:23,397
<i>Star Wars</i> on BIu-ray.

8
00:00:23,564 --> 00:00:25,732
Haven't you seen that movie
a thousand times?

9
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:27,568
Not on BIu-ray.

10
00:00:28,277 --> 00:00:30,279
Only twice on BIu-ray.

11
00:00:30,988 --> 00:00:32,197
Oh, Leonard. Ugh.

12
00:00:32,365 --> 00:00:36,535
LEONARD:
I know. It's high-resolution sadness.

13
00:00:36,702 --> 00:00:39,287
Well, I was gonna take myself out
to a movie tonight.

14
00:00:39,455 --> 00:00:40,581
You wanna go?

15
00:00:40,790 --> 00:00:43,209
-Really? Do we do that?
-What do you mean?

16
00:00:43,376 --> 00:00:46,796
You know, we haven't spent time alone
together since we broke up.

17
00:00:46,963 --> 00:00:49,966
It's not a date, Leonard.
It's a man and a woman hanging out...

18
00:00:50,132 --> 00:00:52,843
...not having sex
at the end of the night.

19
00:00:53,427 --> 00:00:55,929
LEONARD:
Sounds like most of my dates.

20
00:00:57,807 --> 00:01:01,060
SHELDON: Oh, dear Lord.
Get away from me, you monster.

21
00:01:01,227 --> 00:01:03,312
What is that about?

22
00:01:03,479 --> 00:01:07,232
He's smart and crazy enough.
He may have actually created a monster.

23
00:01:08,025 --> 00:01:09,234
Shoo,shoo.

24
00:01:09,402 --> 00:01:10,569
Be gone.

25
00:01:10,736 --> 00:01:12,028
What the hell is going on?

26
00:01:12,196 --> 00:01:15,032
There's a bird outside the window
and he won't go away.

27
00:01:15,199 --> 00:01:17,326
That is the hell that is going on.

28
00:01:17,994 --> 00:01:21,247
We have no worms or seeds here.
Shoo,shoo.

29
00:01:22,498 --> 00:01:25,334
Really? On top of everything else,
you're afraid of birds?

30
00:01:25,501 --> 00:01:29,880
It's called ornithophobia, and someday it
will be recognized as a true disability...

31
00:01:30,047 --> 00:01:34,547
...and the landlord will be required by
law to put a giant net over the building.

32
00:01:35,177 --> 00:01:38,180
Which is unfortunate,
because I have a fear of nets.

33
00:01:38,973 --> 00:01:40,766
80 movies, yes or no?

34
00:01:40,933 --> 00:01:42,517
-Oh, movies, yes.
PENNY: Mm.

35
00:01:42,685 --> 00:01:45,854
Great. I'll see you later.
And remember, he's more afraid of you...

36
00:01:46,022 --> 00:01:47,773
-...than you are of him.
-That doesn't help.

37
00:01:47,940 --> 00:01:49,024
PENNY:
Oh.

38
00:01:49,191 --> 00:01:51,568
I was talking to the bird.

39
00:01:52,695 --> 00:01:53,904
