235
00:14:29,618 --> 00:14:31,494
Hiking.

236
00:14:32,704 --> 00:14:34,622
Karaoke in Koreatown.

237
00:14:36,041 --> 00:14:38,877
Any Jennifer Anniston movie.

238
00:14:39,419 --> 00:14:42,422
-Hey, sorry I ditched you.
-No, it's fine. Ditch away.

239
00:14:42,589 --> 00:14:44,424
Oh, no.
We were gonna hang out. Let's hang out.

240
00:14:44,591 --> 00:14:47,802
-It's cool. Go back to Kevin.
-No, he had to leave.

241
00:14:47,969 --> 00:14:49,178
Interesting.

242
00:14:49,346 --> 00:14:51,806
So now that he's gone,
you wanna hang out with me.

243
00:14:51,973 --> 00:14:53,391
-This must be Penny.
-Yep.

244
00:14:53,558 --> 00:14:55,560
I totally get it.

245
00:14:59,022 --> 00:15:01,357
-Uh, I'm sorry. Get what?
-Don't worry about it.

246
00:15:01,525 --> 00:15:03,485
There's guys over there.
Go talk to them.

247
00:15:03,652 --> 00:15:07,572
-No, no. I wanna know what you told her.
-That's kind of between me and....

248
00:15:07,739 --> 00:15:09,532
-Laura.
-Laura.

249
00:15:09,699 --> 00:15:12,410
Oh, okay, I see.
80 while he was telling you things...

250
00:15:12,577 --> 00:15:16,372
...did he mention he owns not one,
but two <i>Star</i> Trek uniforms?

251
00:15:16,915 --> 00:15:18,374
-Really?
-Yeah. Wears them.

252
00:15:18,542 --> 00:15:20,710
Not just for Halloween.

253
00:15:22,462 --> 00:15:24,172
Hey, pal.

254
00:15:25,799 --> 00:15:28,718
You didn't see me telling Kevin
that you thought cold wars...

255
00:15:28,885 --> 00:15:31,387
...were only fought in winter.

256
00:15:31,930 --> 00:15:33,598
Okay, then I'll return the favor...

257
00:15:33,765 --> 00:15:36,058
-...and I won't tell--
-Laura.

258
00:15:36,226 --> 00:15:40,726
--Laura that half the dirty movies
you own are animated.

259
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:47,987
When you were telling Kevin
about your acting career...

260
00:15:48,196 --> 00:15:50,823
...did you mention your long-running
role as waitress...

261
00:15:50,991 --> 00:15:54,411
...in a local production
of The Cheesecake Factory?

262
00:15:55,454 --> 00:15:57,789
Did you tell her
about your lucky asthma inhaler?

263
00:15:59,124 --> 00:16:01,334
Oh, yeah? Spell asthma.

264
00:16:03,503 --> 00:16:06,005
A-S....

265
00:16:06,214 --> 00:16:07,965
Take me home.

266
00:16:08,133 --> 00:16:09,759
Maybe I'm not done hanging out--

267
00:16:12,929 --> 00:16:15,222
You're right, it's getting late.

268
00:16:20,896 --> 00:16:22,689
It's remarkable.

269
00:16:22,856 --> 00:16:26,901
All that time spent in fear. For what?

270
00:16:27,068 --> 00:16:29,236
He's magnificent.

271
00:16:30,030 --> 00:16:34,530
Ah! Oh, dear. I just realized
I haven't offered you a beverage.

272
00:16:40,999 --> 00:16:44,752
Aw, it's just like my grandma
with her parrot.

273
00:16:45,086 --> 00:16:48,339
And after she lost her marbles,
with her remote control.

274
00:16:50,467 --> 00:16:54,888
My phone's on the desk over there.
Take a picture of us together.

275
00:16:55,055 --> 00:16:58,767
Make it good enough to go on a mug,
a mouse pad and a calendar.

276
00:17:04,481 --> 00:17:07,150
If you were a dove,
I'd call you Lovey Dovey.

277
00:17:07,317 --> 00:17:11,404
Oh, who am I kidding? This isn't a moment
for strict adherence to the literal.

278
00:17:11,571 --> 00:17:14,323
You're just my little Lovey Dovey,
aren't you?

279
00:17:15,784 --> 00:17:19,579
I guess you gotta have hollow bones
to get some sugar around here.

280
00:17:22,082 --> 00:17:24,501
I still think
he looks like someone's pet.

281
00:17:24,668 --> 00:17:26,211
Maybe we should put up posters.

282
00:17:26,378 --> 00:17:29,631
Yes, it should have a big picture of him
and the words:

283
00:17:29,798 --> 00:17:33,426
"Is this your bird? Not anymore."

284
00:17:35,679 --> 00:17:37,472
We're gonna have
so much fun together.

285
00:17:37,639 --> 00:17:40,016
You can carry messages
to all my enemies.

286
00:17:40,225 --> 00:17:41,267
And, um....

287
00:17:41,434 --> 00:17:45,646
I can tie a string to your leg
and fly you like a kite.

288
00:17:45,814 --> 00:17:48,399
If you're keeping him,
I've got a cage you can borrow.

289
00:17:48,567 --> 00:17:52,529
One of the test monkeys slipped
on a banana peel and broke his neck.

290
00:17:53,113 --> 00:17:56,199
It was both tragic and hysterical.

291
00:17:58,618 --> 00:18:02,622
Nonsense. No, Lovey Dovey
doesn't sleep in a cage.

292
00:18:02,831 --> 00:18:06,125
No, Lovey Dovey sleeps
in his very own nest...

293
00:18:06,334 --> 00:18:09,837
...which I'm going to get off
the window sill and put in my room.

294
00:18:10,005 --> 00:18:12,507
Isn't that right, L.D.?

295
00:18:16,636 --> 00:18:17,803
No.

296
00:18:17,971 --> 00:18:19,430
Where are you going?

297
00:18:19,598 --> 00:18:23,018
Come back, Lovey Dovey.
This is your home now.

298
00:18:23,184 --> 00:18:27,271
I already ordered 20 pounds
of bird feed off of Amazon.

299
00:18:29,107 --> 00:18:32,443
-He's gone.
-I'm sorry, Sheldon.

300
00:18:32,611 --> 00:18:34,571
How could he do this to me?

301
00:18:35,405 --> 00:18:39,158
Get back here you stupid bird
so I can love you!

302
00:19:03,350 --> 00:19:04,893
[PENNY SIGHS]

303
00:19:13,151 --> 00:19:15,111
[BOTH SIGH]

304
00:19:15,278 --> 00:19:18,572
Okay, so we went out, saw a movie...

305
00:19:18,740 --> 00:19:22,285
...met some nice people, said horrible
things about each other in public.

306
00:19:22,452 --> 00:19:25,288
All in all, a pretty magical night.

307
00:19:25,455 --> 00:19:28,666
PENNY: Okay, I'm not innocent in all this,
but you basically called me stupid...

308
00:19:28,833 --> 00:19:31,710
...you asthmatic dumb-ass.

309
00:19:32,587 --> 00:19:36,549
I know, uh, I crossed the line.
And I'm sorry.

310
00:19:36,716 --> 00:19:40,219
And no, no, uh, I really mean it.
It's not like when we were going out...

311
00:19:40,428 --> 00:19:43,639
...I'd just apologize for everything
so we could end up in bed.

312
00:19:44,808 --> 00:19:49,308
This is a 100 percent
"sex is off the table" I'm sorry.

313
00:19:50,355 --> 00:19:52,940
All right. Thank you. I'm sorry too.

314
00:19:53,858 --> 00:19:56,819
Just to be clear,
sex is off the table, right?

315
00:19:57,737 --> 00:19:59,613
Way off.

316
00:20:01,449 --> 00:20:03,701
Maybe we're not ready to hang out
as friends.

317
00:20:03,868 --> 00:20:05,744
I don't know. Up until the last part...

318
00:20:05,954 --> 00:20:09,207
...I was enjoying take-charge Leonard
with a little backbone.

319
00:20:09,749 --> 00:20:13,586
Picking the movie,
knowing what he wants, a little cocky.

320
00:20:13,753 --> 00:20:15,171
-Really?
-Yeah.

321
00:20:15,964 --> 00:20:19,467
Well, then, I'm putting sex
back on the table.

322
00:20:21,094 --> 00:20:22,303
[LEONARD CHUCKLES]

323
00:20:22,470 --> 00:20:24,763
What do you think about that?

324
00:20:24,931 --> 00:20:26,557
Hmm, maybe I like it.

325
00:20:26,725 --> 00:20:30,770
If that's what you like, I can be that guy.
I'll be anything you want me to be.

326
00:20:31,813 --> 00:20:32,855
Good night, Leonard.

327
00:20:33,022 --> 00:20:34,314
[LEONARD SIGHS]

328
00:20:35,692 --> 00:20:37,193
[DOOR OPENS THEN CLOSES]

329
00:20:37,360 --> 00:20:40,988
I am such an asthmatic dumb-ass.

330
00:20:42,866 --> 00:20:44,450
I had a weird night.

331
00:20:44,617 --> 00:20:46,577
Mine was great.

332
00:20:46,745 --> 00:20:49,581
I'm going to be a mommy.

333
00:21:18,443 --> 00:21:20,445
[English - US - SDH]

